# Copy to .env (git-ignored) and restart NETVISTA. Every line is optional.
# Comments go on their own lines (a "#" after a value would become part of the value).
#
# --- Free: Google Gemini as primary, Groq as backup -------------------------------------------
# Gemini key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey    Groq key: https://console.groq.com/keys
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# NETVISTA_AI_PROVIDER=gemini
# NETVISTA_AI_BACKUP=groq
# NETVISTA_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash
# NETVISTA_GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
# (The backup answers when the primary is rate-limited, down or rejects its key; the primary then
#  rests for 60 s. NETVISTA_AI_BACKUP=none disables it, =ollama uses a local model instead.)
#
# --- Claude: an API key from https://console.anthropic.com ------------------------------------
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# Model (default claude-opus-5-5; claude-sonnet-5-5 or claude-haiku-5-5 are cheaper and faster)
# NETVISTA_AI_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
#
# --- Local: Ollama -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without any key, a local Ollama server is used if one is running (any model with tool support,
# e.g. `ollama pull qwen3:8b`). Force a provider, or switch the copilot off:
# NETVISTA_AI_PROVIDER=anthropic|gemini|groq|ollama|off
# NETVISTA_OLLAMA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434
# NETVISTA_OLLAMA_NUM_CTX=12288
